    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d597">

                <pb facs="0825" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-05T10:00:00+07:00">September 5,
                            1944—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10: 55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1502. Central News Agency despatch Tihwa, September 2, reports that General Chu
                    Shao-liang arrived in Tihwa August 31 and assumed post of acting Chairman of the
                    Sinkiang Provincial Government September 2; and that Sheng Shih-tsai is to leave
                    Tihwa shortly for Chungking to assume post of Minister of Agriculture and
                    Forestry.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
